  "question": {
    "text": "In the experiment to determine the galvanometer resistance by half-deflection method, the plot of $1 / \\theta$ vs the resistance $(\\mathrm{R})$ of the resistance box is shown in the figure. The figure of merit of the galvanometer is _____ $\\times 10^{-1} \\mathrm{~A} /$ division. [The source has emf 2V]\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/kB35SHNcwsXRJbU2LuzX-9nool1GhvSvwmK44f2klt0.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & i=K \\theta \\\\ & \\frac{2}{G+R}=K \\theta \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{\\theta}=\\frac{(G+R) K}{2}=R\\left(\\frac{K}{2}\\right)+\\frac{K G}{2} \\\\ & \\text { Slope }=\\frac{K}{2}=\\frac{1}{4} \\Rightarrow K=0.5=5 \\times 10^{-1} A\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
